Key a Claude account by user and organization.

Source: omacom/omarchy pull request 18681 (head 560ce87ad93b), the bin/ part only, reconciled
here with quattro's login seating and collector locking at a490d5bdb (the omarchy-dev
4.0.0.r8044 build), plus one change: signing in again as an account also checks the
organization (from its login's profile when an older registry entry has none), and never takes
a login that is already another registered account's.
The same change as pull request 16144, carried onto quattro. Commits 9806db5f
and 35148783 by Michele Di Giovanni (mikjkd), d0cbc870 by Viktor Tar (viktortar98), 07fb5230
and 560ce87a by Omarchybot.
License: as Omarchy (MIT).

Why here: the agents panel keys a Claude account by the claude.ai user alone, so one user in
two organizations (a personal plan and a Team) cannot add the second one ("That's Main ...").
Applied to /usr/bin by linux/omarchy-patches-apply: exactly, or as a three-way merge against
0001-claude-account-by-user-and-organization.base/, the files it was written for.
Retire this file once Omarchy ships the fix (see docs/omarchy-patches.md).

